{%- comment -%}
  IVORY / WINE — light ladder, deep burgundy accent.

  Two deliberate departures from the other schemes, both of them
  the reason this scheme exists:

  1. The accent is wine, not gold. Wine #762B36 reads 9.7:1 on
     white and 9.0:1 on the paper rung, but only 1.97:1 on the
     s4 contrast band — unreadable. So --gold carries the accent
     for the three light rungs and --gold-light carries the
     lightened wine used on s4, which is exactly the split the
     gold schemes already use.

  2. The primary button is ink, not accent. Wine stays for
     labels, rules and small marks; the button is near-black
     with paper text. --on-gold therefore ships white, because
     white is what is legible on a wine fill.
{%- endcomment -%}
